    "title": "Distinguish enough from necessary",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-sufficient-necessary-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Distinguish enough from necessary",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "只要…就… presents a condition as sufficient for the stated outcome; it need not be the only way. 只有…才… presents a necessary condition: without it, the outcome does not hold, but meeting it alone is not automatically a promise of the outcome.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "只要你有时间，我们就能见面。",
                "pinyin": "zhǐyào nǐ yǒu shíjiān ， wǒmen jiù néng jiànmiàn 。",
                "meaning": "As long as you have time, we can meet.",
                "audio": "cc054dcefb270a5ae7b1e04b279f967d69e6859217fa8a6c5b41b276cb264d60"
              },
              {
                "text": "只有你来，我才去。",
                "pinyin": "zhǐyǒu nǐ lái ， wǒ cái qù 。",
                "meaning": "Only if you come will I go.",
                "audio": "048d9aea2e873174db76b9b307ba21ab8f2a4965250ff19f118c12128373cbbf"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "只要",
                "pinyin": "zhǐyào",
                "meaning": "so long as; provided",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "419350402fe7e8fe1dd51e10941c810e3a23456d65bf76646371d0f6912a90cf"
              },
